  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "When we subtract a positive number from a negative number, we move towards the left on the number line. \n\nFor example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n-1 - 6\n$$\n\nTo subtract $6$ from $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on the number line and move $6$ places to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14147971/assets/27f1ec50826854059d1794b7f449704e084688437f7fecd64ff23de65a081343.png)\n\nWhen we do this, we land at $-7.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n-1-6 = -7.\n$$",
